{"source":{"book":"Genesis","name":"Open Scriptures Hebrew Bible","attribution":"Original work of the Open Scriptures Hebrew Bible available at https://github.com/openscriptures/morphhb","license":"CC BY 4.0 (tagging); the Westminster Leningrad Codex text is in the public domain"},"patterns":[{"id":"lexical","group":"lexical","label":"Lexical Form","explain":"The interrogative ה takes its lexical form, הֲ, before any non-guttural consonant that has a vowel."},{"id":"guttural_no_qamets","group":"guttural_no_qamets","label":"Guttural without ◌ָ","explain":"Before a guttural that has a vowel other than qameṣ or qameṣ-ḥaṭuf, the interrogative ה takes pataḥ: הַ."},{"id":"vocal_sheva","group":"vocal_sheva","label":"Vocal Sheva","explain":"Before any consonant that has a vocal sheva, the interrogative ה takes pataḥ: הַ."},{"id":"guttural_qamets","group":"guttural_qamets","label":"Guttural with ◌ָ","explain":"Before a guttural that has a qameṣ or qameṣ-ḥaṭuf, the interrogative ה takes segol: הֶ."}],"groups":[{"id":"lexical","label":"Lexical Form","patterns":["lexical"]},{"id":"guttural_no_qamets","label":"Guttural w/out ◌ָ","patterns":["guttural_no_qamets"]},{"id":"vocal_sheva","label":"Vocal Sheva","patterns":["vocal_sheva"]},{"id":"guttural_qamets","label":"Guttural w/ ◌ָ","patterns":["guttural_qamets"]}],"table":[{"form":"הֲ","rule":"Before any non-guttural consonant that has a vowel.","article":"הַ + a dagesh forte in the first letter of the noun","note":"The interrogative has no dagesh; the article doubles the next letter."},{"form":"הַ","rule":"Before a guttural that has a vowel other than qameṣ or qameṣ-ḥaṭuf.","article":"הַ (implicit doubling), or הָ (compensatory lengthening) before א, ר or ע","note":"The two can look identical: the interrogative keeps its pataḥ, while the article’s guttural rejects the dagesh."},{"form":"הַ","rule":"Before any consonant that has a vocal sheva.","article":"הַ + a dagesh forte, which may be lost before a SQNMLVY consonant with a voc